# Local-only files. None of this is part of the web build, and uploading it
# turns a deploy into a 40+ MB transfer that fails on a flaky connection.
#
# Scope every rule to a directory. A bare `*.png` / `*.md` glob here silently
# strips public/brand/* from the upload and the live site starts 404-ing on
# its own logo, so never match media extensions globally.
android/
telegram-agent/
scripts/
docs/
tests/

# Screenshots and recordings captured locally, not shipped assets.
*.log
*.mp4
*.webm

# NOTE: a bare `*.apk` used to sit here and silently stripped
# marketing-site/public/downloads/azura-app.apk — the artefact /download
# serves. The live download 404-ed while the local build looked perfect.
# The only other APK in the repo is under android/, which is already
# excluded by its own directory rule, so nothing needs the glob. The
# negation below is kept as a guard in case another shipped APK appears.
!marketing-site/public/downloads/*.apk

# Only ever excluded in the repo root, never inside public/.
/README.local.md